Package: clee
Version: @VERSION@
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: Matteo Savoia <matteo.savoia@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://cleecode.marunja.com
Description: terminal IDE that works over ssh with zero configuration
 CleeCode is one binary: an editor, a file tree and real terminals in one
 window, written in Rust and driven from the keyboard, with the mouse as an
 alternative rather than the only way. It wants no server on the far end of
 an ssh session and no configuration file to be useful on the first run.
 .
 The command is clee. The package ships the binary, its man page and a
 desktop entry that launches it in a terminal.
